%% alt: The request path through the primer's components. A user's request passes through the gateway (3.1), input guardrails (3.2) and context engineering (3.3), then retrieval (3.4 to 3.6) and a workflow or agent (3.9 to 3.11), reaches the model layer (3.7, 3.8), and returns through output checks (3.12). Caching, asynchronism, evals, observability and security support the path.
flowchart TB
  U[User]:::human --> G[Gateway 3.1]:::control --> IG[Input guardrails 3.2]:::control --> C[Context engineering 3.3]:::tool
  C --> R[Retrieval 3.4–3.6]:::data & A[Workflow or agent 3.9–3.11]:::tool
  R & A --> M[Model layer 3.7–3.8]:::model
  M --> OG[Output checks 3.12]:::control
  OG -.->|answer| U
  M ~~~ X[Across the path:<br/>caching 3.13<br/>async 3.14<br/>evals 3.15<br/>observability 3.16<br/>security 3.17]
